    "created_at": "2020-12-24T05:33:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-24T05:33:23Z",
    "body": "DNS is non-normative for HTTP. The standards display some verbal dexterity to avoid actually specifying or recommending the use of DNS for address resolution, let alone how it is used.\r\n\r\nErgo, a header that purports to amends how it is used, has nothing to amend, from a standards perspective.\r\n\r\nThere have been numerous attempts to fix this particular elephant-in-the-room. The most recent draft being https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-dnsop-svcb-httpssvc-03, I think - now expired.\r\n",
